  "body": "## What changed\n\n`assets/posts/haas.cps`, `onCycle`: the open-cycle signature was `g|Z|R|Q` for G82 and G89. When two holes in one open group had different dwells, the second hole was posted as a bare `X Y` block and ran the first hole's modal P. That is wrong posted G-code (P1).\n\n- The dwell is now part of the signature for G82, G83 and G89. #2048 already did this for G83, and the code now covers the three dwell cycles together. When the dwell changes, the post writes `G80` and issues the cycle again with the new hole's own P.\n- G89 now always writes P, and writes `P0` for a zero dwell. Without it, a reissued G89 would pick up the old modal P (Haas G04/G83 documentation: P is modal). G82 is chosen only for a positive dwell (a zero-dwell drill posts G81), so G82 always carries its P already.\n- Holes with the same dwell stay in the open group as bare `X Y` blocks, as before.\n\nHaas output changes only when G82/G89 holes in one group have different dwells, or for a zero-dwell G89, which gains `P0`. No existing golden changes: `synth_haas.nc` has one G82 that already writes `P500`, and no G89.\n\nThe change stays inside the Haas post. It follows #2048's G83 approach: dwell in the signature, P0 clears the modal dwell. It does not touch the files of #2351 (grblHAL/Tormach) or the Sinumerik post (#2349).\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/2350-haas-g82-g89-dwell.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew pin `crates/post/tests/haas_dwell_cycles.rs`:\n- `haas_g82_rewrites_p_when_the_dwell_changes`: two G82 holes, 0.5 s then 0.75 s, give P500 then P750.\n- `haas_g89_rewrites_p_when_the_dwell_changes`: the same for G89.\n- `haas_g89_zero_dwell_writes_p0`: G89 with 0.5 s then 0 s gives P500 then P0; a single zero-dwell G89 gives P0.\n- `haas_same_dwell_keeps_the_open_group`: with an unchanged dwell, the second hole is still a bare X Y block.\n\nOn the old `haas.cps`, the first three fail (the second hole had no P, `[Some(\"P500\"), None]`). With the fix all four pass.\n\nQuick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 66 steps, 0 failed (includes post suites haas_dwell_cycles, g83_dwell, script_haas and the app post suites). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo real Haas control was run. Haas's G85 still writes a positive P, which this PR leaves alone (out of scope, #1445).\n\nChangelog: Haas post: G82 and G89 holes in one cycle group now each post their own dwell P (a changed dwell reissues the cycle; a zero-dwell G89 writes P0) instead of running the previous hole's modal dwell (#2350)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #2350\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
